<!--/Post: 10417-->
<!--Post: 10587--><!--Time: 1110036503-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10587"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 7:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that Nola said at the press conference that the entire case would be sealed! I would really like to read those affidavit&#39;s if they are public record. I&#39;m sure a gag order will prevent that from happening. <BR> <BR>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/11058178.htm <!--/Text--></td></tr>
