<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13166"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 9:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->New Details About The BTK Case Could Soon Be Made Public  <BR>Cara Kumari <BR> <BR>Since the arrest of Dennis Rader, there has been much secrecy involving the BTK suspect, and the case against him. But that could soon change. <BR> <BR>We know that motions have been filed in the Rader case, we just don&#39;t know what they are. That&#39;s because everything filed with the courts so far has been sealed. <BR> <BR>But according to the Wichita Eagle, both the prosecution and defense have agreed not all future records need to be sealed. And previous seals are being reviewed to see whether they can be made public. <BR> <BR>See rest of article and video called &#34;New Details About The BTK Case Could Soon Be Made Public&#34; at the website: <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1506297.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1506297.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13166-->
<!--Post: 13168--><!--Time: 1114446587-->
